Keep the encoder's plane views across frames.

pyrowave_encoder_encode_gpu() wraps the three plane images and creates three
image views on every call, and the frame context destroys them again. The
host passes the same three imported planes every frame, so the views only
change when it rebuilds the planes for a new capture format or size.

The views now live on the encoder and are wrapped again only when a plane
changes. Unlike Punktfunk's version, a plane is identified by an id the
device gives each pyrowave_image, not by its VkImage handle alone. The host
destroys and recreates its planes when the capture format changes, and
pyrowave_image_destroy() pumps the frame contexts, so the old VkImages can
be freed before the new ones are created and the driver may hand back the
same handle; a handle-only key would then bind a view of the freed image.
Planes of images pyrowave_image_create() did not make are still wrapped for
each frame.

From Punktfunk patch 0010 (encoder-cached-plane-views).
